The note doesn't fit the example assertion, so I'm keeping my earlier answer. A union would return `{3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10}`, not `{4, 5}`. Comparing by index with `zip` would find no matches for `(3, 4, 5, 6)` and `(5, 7, 4, 10)`, so it returns an empty result. Only the set intersection gives `{4, 5}`.

```python
def similar_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):
    return tuple(set(test_tup1) & set(test_tup2))
```

